  <h1>A Bitter Lesson for Data Filtering</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Filtering training data to keep only "high-quality" content is almost universally assumed to be necessary for LLM pretraining. Stanford researchers challenge this: with enough compute and large enough models, <em>no filter</em> outperforms every standard filter — and models even benefit from shuffled-word junk.
  </p>
